// Declaration: This file is partially AI-generated and reviewed by human.
// namely, the AI wired the benchmark-related code segments in, and
// wrote the argument parsing, i.e. mostly benchmarking and peripherals.
// runner_main.cpp — auto-generated by lower_to_timvx.py. Edits welcome,
// the next regeneration will overwrite. The script substitutes four
// markers (BASE, FUNC_NAME, INPUT_SPECS, INPUT_ARGS) at the appropriate
// places below.
//
// Run modes
// =========
//
//   1. one-shot (legacy):
//        runner <input0.bin> [<input1.bin> ...]
//      One inference, print summary, exit. argv blobs are raw MLIR-row-
//      major bytes, one per non-graph function argument.
//
//   2. one-shot via orchestrator (CPU pre/post folded around NPU):
//        runner --mode <mode-name> <input0.bin> [<input1.bin> ...]
//      Same single inference but routed through the configurable
//      orchestrator — primarily useful when paired with `--bench`.
//
//   3. benchmark:
//        runner --mode <mode-name> --bench <N> <input0.bin> ...
//      Submits N copies of the input through the selected orchestrator
//      to measure throughput. Modes: 4 orchestration strategies ×
//      4 pre/post backends — see `pipeline/factory.h`.
//
//      mode-name ∈ {cpu-*, cpu_zero_copy-*, ppu-*, ppu_zero_copy-*}
//                  × {-sequential, -pipeline, -pool, -hybrid}
//
//   4. eval (one-time accuracy sweep):
//        runner --eval-dir <dir> --labels <file.json>
//               [--limit <N>] [--passthrough]
//      Walks the dir of JPEGs (or .bin tensors with --passthrough) and
//      accumulates top-1 / top-5 against labels[stem]. Hardcoded to
//      mode=cpu-sequential. Plumbing in `pipeline/eval.h`.
//
// All pipeline plumbing lives under `pipeline/` headers. This file only
// declares the auto-generated `kInputs` and dispatches argv into one of
// the four run modes above.

